{"If multiple requests happen before the first one hits the database, all will cache true before any limit check occurs": 0.5607802867889404, "Authentication failure behavior on ErrDeviceLimitReached needs clarification - conflicting requirements on whether authentication should fail when device limit is reached": 0.33832472562789917, "updateDevice method returns ErrDeviceLimitReached when rowsAffected == 0, but this condition indicates the device wasn't found or timestamp check failed, not that a device limit was reached - semantically incorrect error": 0.7158366441726685, "Data loss occurs because new devices cannot be added once limit is reached, and old devices cannot be updated if they fall outside the 30-day time window": 0.45690980553627014, "Local cache in tagDeviceUI conflates 'we called the database' with 'the limit allows this device' - cache value true/false is sticky and doesn't expire based on actual limit status": 0.4714214503765106, "If device limit is later increased or devices are deleted, the cache will continue blocking valid requests": 0.4918077290058136}